 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "When a microwave appears completely dead with no lights or sounds, it is often due to simple power issues, a control lock being active, or a fault with the door interlock switches. To help narrow this down, please first check that the plug is firmly in the socket and try plugging another appliance into that same socket to confirm there is power. Also, look for any key or lock symbol on the display indicating a child lock might be engaged, which can prevent operation."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "it's not completely dead, display is on and it beeps. there's a little L symbol on the display though"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That little L symbol usually means the control lock is on, which stops the buttons from working even though the display and beeps are active. This is often just a settings issue rather than a hardware fault. Please try holding down the Stop or Cancel button for about three seconds to see if it turns off. If that doesn't work, check your manual for a specific key combination like 'Lock' or 'Menu' to disable it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok tried holding Stop for 3 secs, the L went away and it works now. thanks"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That's great news! It sounds like you've sorted out the control lock issue perfectly. To prevent this from happening again, just remember to check for that 'L' symbol if the buttons stop responding in the future. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
